triage: fix_game: The interface defines `ending_triggered` as true only once some player has emptied their hand. In the 3-player cycle-limit scenario no hand was empty (sizes 3, 2, 2), yet the game set it to True when `cycle` reached `max_cycles` = 12. The game is reusing that flag for the cycle-limit ending, so the test's expectation of False is correct.
step C: building the game file
step D: evaluating
triage: revise_rules: The game is built and behaves as specified, yet one fixed, thoughtless policy wins about 90% of decided matches and the opposite fixed policy loses nearly every game. The real decisions are degenerate: playing a card off your hand is almost always right, and taking a pile is almost always wrong, so little strategy remains.
